{
  "name": "sastquatch-reviewer-arc",
  "version": 1,
  "vars_schema": {
    "owner":         { "kind": "string", "required": true },
    "repo":          { "kind": "string", "required": true },
    "pr_number":     { "kind": "int",    "required": true },
    "work_item_id":  { "kind": "string" },
    "work_packet":   { "kind": "object" },
    "pr_diff":       { "kind": "any" },
    "review_payload":{ "kind": "object" },
    "feedback_posted": { "kind": "bool" }
  },
  "actors": {
    "reviewers": {
      "kind": "ensemble",
      "team": "sastquatch-reviewers",
      "durable": false,
      "requires": []
    },
    "aggregator": {
      "kind": "executor",
      "brofile": "sastquatch-review",
      "durable": false,
      "requires": []
    }
  },
  "start": "FetchDiff",
  "nodes": {
    "FetchDiff": {
      "actor": "",
      "prompt": "Mechanical PR diff fetch.",
      "on_enter": [
        {
          "op": "http_json",
          "args": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "${env.FORGEJO_BASE_URL}/api/v1/repos/${vars.owner}/${vars.repo}/pulls/${vars.pr_number}.diff",
            "headers": {
              "Authorization": "token ${env.FORGEJO_TOKEN}",
              "Accept": "text/plain"
            },
            "response_kind": "text",
            "allow_empty_body": true
          },
          "into_var": "pr_diff",
          "on_failure": "halt"
        }
      ],
      "next": { "type": "goto", "to": "Review" }
    },
    "Review": {
      "actor": "reviewers",
      "prompt": "PR #${vars.pr_number} on ${vars.owner}/${vars.repo} addresses SAST cluster '${vars.work_packet.cluster_title}' (dimension=${vars.work_packet.dimension}, ${vars.work_packet.finding_count} findings).\n\nORIGINAL CLUSTER RATIONALE (from triager):\n${vars.work_packet.rationale}\n\nFIX BRIEF:\n${vars.work_packet.fix_brief}\n\nDIFF:\n${vars.pr_diff}\n\nReview against:\n  1. Does the diff actually address the cluster as described?\n  2. Did it introduce any new SAST findings (regression)?\n  3. Is the fix minimal and focused, or does it sprawl?\n  4. Any obvious correctness issues, edge cases, or incorrect logic?\n\nReturn ONE LINE — exactly one of:\n  APPROVE\n  REQUEST CHANGES: <one-paragraph specific feedback>\n\nBe terse. The aggregator combines all reviewer lines into one PR review.",
      "next": { "type": "goto", "to": "Aggregate" }
    },
    "Aggregate": {
      "actor": "aggregator",
      "prompt": "Aggregate the reviewer round into ONE structured review payload for PR #${vars.pr_number}.\n\nPRIOR ROUND OUTPUTS (one block per reviewer):\n${Review.output}\n\nReturn STRICT JSON — no surrounding prose, no markdown fences:\n{\n  \"event\": \"COMMENT\",\n  \"body\": \"<one-to-three-sentence aggregate; lead with APPROVE or REQUEST CHANGES then the reasoning>\",\n  \"action\": \"merge\" | \"request_changes\"\n}\n\nUse action=merge ONLY when every reviewer line was APPROVE. Otherwise action=request_changes. event is always COMMENT (this demo runs single-user; Forgejo refuses APPROVED/REQUEST_CHANGES on own PRs). The PostReview node reads `action` to decide whether to auto-merge.",
      "next": { "type": "goto", "to": "PostReview" }
    },
    "PostReview": {
      "actor": "",
      "prompt": "Mechanical: parse the aggregator's JSON, post the PR review, merge if approved, log to the work-item thread.",
      "on_enter": [
        {
          "op": "parse_json",
          "args": { "from": "${Aggregate.output}" },
          "into_var": "review_payload",
          "on_failure": "halt"
        },
        {
          "op": "http_json",
          "args": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": "${env.FORGEJO_BASE_URL}/api/v1/repos/${vars.owner}/${vars.repo}/pulls/${vars.pr_number}/reviews",
            "headers": {
              "Authorization": "token ${env.FORGEJO_TOKEN}",
              "Accept": "application/json",
              "Content-Type": "application/json"
            },
            "body": {
              "event": "${vars.review_payload.event}",
              "body":  "${vars.review_payload.body}"
            },
            "expect_status": [200, 201]
          },
          "on_failure": "halt"
        },
        {
          "op": "http_json",
          "args": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": "${env.FORGEJO_BASE_URL}/api/v1/repos/${vars.owner}/${vars.repo}/pulls/${vars.pr_number}/merge",
            "headers": {
              "Authorization": "token ${env.FORGEJO_TOKEN}",
              "Accept": "application/json",
              "Content-Type": "application/json"
            },
            "body": { "Do": "merge" },
            "expect_status": [200, 201, 204]
          },
          "when": "domain:hook-when/should-merge",
          "on_failure": "halt"
        },
        {
          "op": "mcp_call",
          "args": {
            "server": "blackbox",
            "tool": "bbox_note",
            "arguments": {
              "kind": "learned",
              "body": "Review verdict ${vars.review_payload.action}: ${vars.review_payload.body}",
              "thread_id": "${vars.work_item_id}"
            },
            "timeout_secs": 30
          },
          "when": "domain:hook-when/has-work-item",
          "on_failure": "warn"
        },
        { "op": "set_var", "args": { "key": "feedback_posted", "value": true } }
      ],
      "next": { "type": "terminal" }
    }
  }
}
